# Intent-Based Firewall Rules (Auto-Accept Prior States) POC fixture:
#
# One Prior_State_Rule in `<` operator form targeting DNS, a
# multi-transport protocol (both TCP and UDP are registered upstream).
# The Prior_State pipeline expands this single line into the 10-rule
# set described in design §Worked Example (DNS query allow-list):
# 4 TCP handshake rules + 2 UDP transport rules + 3 DNS prerequisite
# rules + 1 Decision_Hook rule. The input PCAP carries DNS traffic on
# both transports — a UDP query/response pair for `www.amazon.com` and
# a DNS-over-TCP query/response flow (with TCP handshake + teardown)
# for the same name — so both the UDP path (subs 5..6) and the TCP
# path (subs 1..4) are exercised. Both queries match the author's
# `dns.query` condition and fire sid:3003 exactly once each.

accept:tx <dns:request_complete $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET 53 (dns.query; content:".amazon.com"; endswith; sid:3003;)
